  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their own section of `default_map` instead of ignoring it. The cause was in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`: a child context inherited the parent's whole `default_map`. A key like `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` was therefore never found by the subcommand's `port` option. It now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which matches the nested form shown in `docs/commands.md`.\n\nThe existing test suite passes (1906 passed, some skipped). I didn't add a test for this specific case.\n\nOne behavior change: a flat map like `{\"port\": 5000}` on a group no longer reaches the subcommands' options. The nested form is the one the docs describe.",
